# The cast of a defeated Siege (CR 310.12b) is a cast like any other, so "each player can't cast more than one spell each
# turn" (Archon of Emeria, CR 101.2, 601.2) binds it. The setup is the control scenario's, "a defeated siege is cast
# transformed": Bot1's Gorilla takes the Invasion of Gobakhan down to 1 defense on turn 3. Bot2's Archon of Emeria comes down on
# turn 4 (after a Mox Pearl and a Sol Ring, cast while it is not yet out); the Siege's own enter trigger took the Lightning Bolt
# from Bot2's hand, out of the way. On turn 5 Bot1 casts a Mox Jet before combat, and the Gorilla's damage then removes the last counter: the Siege is
# exiled and the transformed cast is not offered (`! Bot1.Accept`), so it stays in exile and the Gorilla gets no counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Guerrilla Gorilla
Plains
Mox Pearl
Invasion of Gobakhan
Plains
Plains
Mox Jet
Plains x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Archon of Emeria
Lightning Bolt
Plains x10

